---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SECTIONS } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="The Unplanned Show is an independent satirical publication about urban planning, public policy and academia.">
  <PageHeader title="About The Unplanned Show" deck="An independent satirical publication about the contradictions of planning." />
  <div class="container doc prose">
    <p>
      The Unplanned Show explores the absurdities, contradictions and unintended consequences of urban planning,
      public policy and academia. It combines factual research, deadpan humor, institutional satire and critical
      commentary.
    </p>
    <blockquote class="principle">Research seriously. Write absurdly. Let the contradiction deliver the punchline.</blockquote>
    <p>
      It does not exist to prove that urban planning is useless. It explores a profession dedicated to shaping
      uncertain futures, and tries to stay informed, curious and willing to question its own assumptions.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is organised</h2>
    <p>Everything is filed as section, then series, then article.</p>
    <ul>
      {SECTIONS.map((s) => <li><a href={withBase(s.href)}>{s.title}</a>: {s.summary}</li>)}
    </ul>

    <h2>Satire and evidence</h2>
    <p>
      The publication is explicitly satirical. Facts are verified, fictional quotations are labelled, and sources
      appear at the foot of each article. Read the full <a href={withBase('/editorial-policy/')}>editorial policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      The publication does not claim to represent a university, government agency, employer or professional
      association. It currently runs as a written blog. Podcast and video formats may follow.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
